# Test files and documentation. LiveReview's own top-level docs/ (engineering
# plans, release notes, etc.) is internal-only and deliberately excluded from
# the image - it is NOT part of the chatbot's RAG corpus (see
# scripts/docindex/sync_docs_sources.sh). internal/docindex/docs/**/*.md is
# re-included below - it's all committed, user-facing RAG/product doc
# content (routes_guide/, plus the synced lr_wiki/lrc_wiki/ .md files) that
# needs to ship in the binary; *.mdx (hexmos_docs/) isn't matched by the
# `*.md` pattern below anyway, so it needs no separate re-inclusion.
#
# This file is Dockerfile.mcp-test's own override of the root .dockerignore
# (buildx picks up "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" automatically): unlike the
# production image, this one *is* the test harness, so tests/ must ship -
# it needs tests/mcp/mcp-testcase.py and tests/mcp/requirements.txt.
docs/
!docs/openapi.yaml
examples/
README.md
*.md
!internal/docindex/docs/**/*.md

# Scripts and tools: exclude known-large local-only artifacts, but keep the
# rest of scripts/ (needed for scripts/docindex/sync_docs_sources.sh +
# scripts/docindex/docs_sources.env, run during the Go builder stage - see
# docs/docs-sources-pinning-plan.md). A blanket `scripts/` exclusion here
# would also hide those from the build context; a Dockerfile COPY can only
# ever see what's already in the context, so exclude specific paths instead.
scripts/.venv/
scripts/prelivi/output/
scripts/prelivi/__pycache__/
scripts/adoption_chart/rca/
scripts/adoption_chart/__pycache__/
scripts/integration/test-results/
scripts/integration/playwright-report/
scripts/gitea_session.json
scripts/mr_details.json
scripts/sample_review_report.json
scripts/pgctl.sh
scripts/setup_local_dev.sh
Makefile*

# Keep docker-entrypoint.sh
!docker-entrypoint.sh

# Chatbot RAG corpus: internal/docindex/docs/{lr_wiki,lrc_wiki,hexmos_docs}/
# and .synced-commits.env are committed to git (see
# docs/docs-sources-pinning-plan.md) - they flow into the build context
# normally via `COPY . .` like any other tracked file, no special exclusion
# needed. scripts/docindex/sync_docs_sources.sh still runs during the Go
# builder stage as a self-heal/freshness check, but is expected to be a
# no-op if the committed content already matches the pinned commits.

# Development containers
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
docker/docker-compose.*.yml
